L0S shell, on an L0 microkernel. Type help for the commands.
l0s>   ls [PATH ...]   every file, or what is in each directory; programs are
                  in /bin, and the disk's volumes in /Volumes
  cat FILE ...    show files
  write FILE WORDS ...
                  make FILE hold WORDS, a line; append adds the line
  cp FROM TO      copy a file, into TO if it is a directory
  mv FROM TO      rename or move a file
  rm FILE ...     remove files
  df              each volume's size, and the room left on it
  format VOLUME   empty a volume, /Volumes/LABEL or LABEL
  ps              the processes running, and what each is doing
  run NAME [ARG ...] [&]
                  run /bin/NAME, or the program at NAME if it holds a /,
                  with ARGs in place of its own; & leaves it running, and
                  Ctrl-C ends one that is not
  wait PID        wait for a process to exit; Ctrl-C stops waiting
  kill PID        end a process, unless it is a driver
  sleep MS        sleep for MS milliseconds
  echo WORDS      print WORDS
  exit [STATUS]   stop the system
